---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About EasyLiife — Independent Insurance Research"
  description="Discover EasyLiife's mission, our consumer research desks, and our transparent 5-pillar insurance evaluation methodology."
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="badge badge-trust">Our Mission & Standards</span>
      <h1>Empowering American Consumers With Transparent Insurance Intelligence</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">
        We dismantle the complexity of auto, home, health, and life insurance policies with verified state rate filings, non-commission reviews, and certified financial expertise.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container page-content">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="grid-2">
        <div>
          <h2>Who We Are</h2>
          <p>
            Founded in 2024, <strong>EasyLiife</strong> is an independent consumer research organization dedicated to bringing radical transparency to the United States insurance marketplace. With over 6,000 licensed insurance companies operating across 50 states, consumers routinely overpay by hundreds—sometimes thousands—of dollars each year simply due to informational opacity.
          </p>
          <p>
            Unlike traditional lead-generation mills that sell your phone number to dozens of telemarketers, EasyLiife was built on an editorial-first principle: <strong>give consumers actionable, data-backed benchmarks before they request a quote</strong>. We aggregate public rate filings from the National Association of Insurance Commissioners (NAIC), cross-reference customer satisfaction indices from J.D. Power, and analyze financial solvency ratings from AM Best to provide real, unvarnished insight.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card-box">
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-num">50+</span>
            <span class="stat-label">National Carriers Monitored</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-num">120K+</span>
            <span class="stat-label">Public Rate Filings Analyzed</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-num">100%</span>
            <span class="stat-label">Reader-First Editorial Policy</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <span class="stat-num">0</span>
            <span class="stat-label">Robocalls Sold</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Editorial Research Desks -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Our Specialized Editorial Research Desks</h2>
        <p>Every guide, calculator model, and coverage comparison on EasyLiife is compiled using publicly available state rate filings, NAIC complaint indices, and official federal regulatory documentation.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="board-grid">
        <div class="board-member card">
          <div class="member-header">
            <div class="member-avatar">PA</div>
            <div>
              <h3>Auto & Property Research Desk</h3>
              <span class="member-role">Personal Lines & State Rate Analysis</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="member-bio">
            Tracks state-level minimum liability mandates, replacement cost valuation formulas, bundling discount structures, and NAIC consumer complaint ratios across major US auto and homeowners insurers.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="board-member card">
          <div class="member-header">
            <div class="member-avatar">LF</div>
            <div>
              <h3>Life & Family Coverage Desk</h3>
              <span class="member-role">Term & Permanent Policy Research</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="member-bio">
            Analyzes term vs. permanent life insurance structures, DIME coverage formulas, underwriting risk tiers, and policy rider trade-offs to help households compare long-term financial protection clearly.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="board-member card">
          <div class="member-header">
            <div class="member-avatar">HM</div>
            <div>
              <h3>Health & Medicare Research Desk</h3>
              <span class="member-role">CMS & ACA Coverage Analysis</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="member-bio">
            Monitors official Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) enrollment calendars, Part D out-of-pocket caps, Medigap plan letters, and ACA marketplace guidelines to keep health guides accurate.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How We Rate Carriers -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Our 5-Pillar Carrier Evaluation Methodology</h2>
      <p>
        We evaluate every insurer across five weighted pillars to produce an objective, balanced score out of 5.0 stars:
      </p>

      <div class="methodology-grid">
        <div class="method-card">
          <div class="method-num">01</div>
          <h4>Financial Solvency (25%)</h4>
          <p>We review AM Best, Fitch, and Standard & Poor’s financial strength ratings to guarantee the insurer can honor claims during catastrophic events.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-card">
          <div class="method-num">02</div>
          <h4>Claim Satisfaction (25%)</h4>
          <p>We analyze the NAIC National Complaint Index (measuring complaints per premium volume) and J.D. Power annual auto and property claims satisfaction studies.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-card">
          <div class="method-num">03</div>
          <h4>Coverage Breadth (20%)</h4>
          <p>We reward carriers that offer robust endorsements—such as OEM parts, accident forgiveness, water backup, and umbrella extensions—without exorbitant markups.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-card">
          <div class="method-num">04</div>
          <h4>Pricing Competitiveness (20%)</h4>
          <p>We analyze thousands of ZIP code rate filings for clean drivers, high-risk motorists, homeowners with varied credit scores, and different family sizes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-card">
          <div class="method-num">05</div>
          <h4>Digital & App Usability (10%)</h4>
          <p>We audit mobile apps, digital claim submission speeds, self-service policy adjustment tools, and 24/7 customer support responsiveness.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Editorial Independence -->
    <section class="section callout">
      <div class="callout-title">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 2C6.48 2 2 6.48 2 12s4.48 10 10 10 10-4.48 10-10S17.52 2 12 2zm1 15h-2v-6h2v6zm0-8h-2V7h2v2z"/></svg>
        Our Editorial Independence Guarantee
      </div>
      <p class="callout-text">
        EasyLiife does not accept payment from insurers to alter carrier ratings, inflate scores, or remove critical editorial findings. While we may receive compensation when consumers click through our links to request quotes or purchase policies, our editorial review team operates independently of commercial partnerships. Our reviews reflect authentic data, regulatory filings, and certified professional scrutiny.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0c1e33 0%, #153252 100%);
    color: #ffffff;
    padding: 3.5rem 0 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 0.75rem;
    max-width: 850px;
  }

  .subtitle {
    color: #cbd5e1;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    max-width: 750px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .page-content {
    max-width: 1000px;
  }

  .section {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .section-heading {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .grid-2 {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 820px) {
    .grid-2 {
      grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
    }
  }

  .stat-card-box {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .stat-card {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    text-align: center;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }

  .stat-num {
    display: block;
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .stat-label {
    font-size: 0.825rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .board-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .board-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .board-member {
    padding: 1.5rem;
  }

  .member-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .member-avatar {
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-primary);
    color: #ffffff;
    font-weight: 700;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .member-header h3 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
  }

  .member-role {
    font-size: 0.775rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    display: block;
  }

  .member-bio {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .methodology-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .methodology-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .method-card {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .method-num {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: #e2e8f0;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .method-card h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .method-card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
